  "result": "I fixed it in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one.\n\nWith an open bound (`min_open` or `max_open`), the clamped value was moved the wrong way, so it landed outside the allowed range. For example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` returned `-1` for an input of `-5`, and the same thing happened on the max side. The code computed `bound - dir`, but it needs to be `bound + dir`. That gives `1` for the min case and `9` for the max case.\n\n`FloatRange` isn't affected because it already rejects clamping with open bounds.",
